course: dictionary
lesson: 12235
title: Considered: thought about carefully
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Considered comes from the verb consider, which means to think about something carefully before you decide. Look for clues that someone has thought hard about something. «Mia considered the offer for a long time before she said yes.» Mia did not say yes at once. She thought about it first, so considered means thought about carefully.
explain: The word also appears in the phrase «is considered to be». «The dog is considered loyal» does not mean someone thought hard about the dog. It means many people believe the dog is loyal. Check the words around it: thinking and deciding point to one meaning, while believing points to the other.
explain: You may also meet considered as a describing word. «Her considered reply was clear and fair» means the answer was thought out with care. The phrase «all things considered» means after thinking about everything: «All things considered, the trip was a good one.»
fact: Considered is the past form of consider: consider, considers, considered, considering.
fact: «Considered» can mean thought about carefully before deciding, as in «He considered his choices».
fact: «Is considered to be» means many people think or believe that something is true, as in «The bridge is considered to be the oldest in town».
fact: A considered opinion is one that has been thought about carefully.
fact: «All things considered» means after thinking about everything.
exercise: «Mia considered the offer for a long time.» What does considered mean here? | Forgotten quickly | Ignored by mistake | Said loudly to everyone | *Thought about carefully before deciding
exercise: «The dog is considered loyal by its owners.» What does is considered mean? | The dog has been sold | The dog is very old | *Many people believe the dog is loyal | The dog is lost
exercise: «Sam considered three ideas before he picked one.» Find and copy the word that shows Sam thought about them. | *considered | Sam | picked | three
test: «All things considered, the trip was a good one.» What does all things considered mean? | Without any thought at all | *After thinking about everything | Only the big things | Quickly, in a rush
test: «Her considered answer was clear and fair.» What does considered tell us about the answer? | It was too short to read | *It was thought about carefully | It was copied from a friend | It was shouted out
exam: «The team is considered to be the best in the league.» What does is considered to be mean? | *Many people believe the team is the best | The team has moved to another town | The team has never won a game | The team is looking for new players
